  "recommendations": {
    "status": "Suggestions only; no candidate authored or accepted.",
    "coordinate_contract": "GLB uses Godot XYZ, Y-up. Node transforms inside these GLBs are identity; actual World Cliffs instances are identity basis plus manifest position (float text rounding only). Control indices below are 0-based. Do not apply Blender coordinate order directly; Blender conversion is (X,-Z,Y).",
    "crown_cause": "front[1..3] project to (1322,699),(1352,702),(1387,699); front[4..5] to (1412,687),(1437,684). This long nearly level transition contributes the waist boundary. Source foot->front strip roles are grass for k=0,1,2,3,6 and wall for k=4,5; front->ridge is all wall. The apparent grass shoulder is therefore largely a green lower slope under a high rock wall, not a separately articulated broad ledge. Color roles are source evidence; visible screen ownership also involves overlapping western_slab/central_wall/terrain, and this audit did not ray-pick GPU pixels.",
    "central_cause": "front[1,2] heights 55/54 and screen y752/753 make a level wall top; front[0..4] connects to mid by nearly straight interpolation: mid=.43front+.57foot, depth offsets only 0,2,-1,2,0 m. Both wall strips share the same control columns. The grass strip front->ridge follows this entire upper contour. Long faces and synchronized boundaries result; the grass wedge cannot be solved by uniform recoloring.",
    "columns_cause": "front[1,2] both height52 and screen (1229,752),(1278,753); back[1,2] heights55/53 project to (1195.208,712.369),(1242.442,721.905). mid=.42front+.58foot plus Z offsets 0,1.2,2.2,0 m gives nearly straight wall columns. The actual cap is already wide in depth (26/24 m centrally); adding blanket thickness would miss the problem. Its top/face heights and depth rhythm need asymmetric organization.",
    "16a_minimal_suggestion": [
      "Freeze every actual seated-rim vertex and every bottom vertex, not only the short authored foot/rear arrays. Audit finds crown110, central71, columns72 distinct seated-rim positions at 5-decimal welding precision. These include side and 4m sampled boundary positions.",
      "First isolate a crown upper-face study: leave ridge[3,4] and rear/bench/rim fixed; adjust front[1..3] height by different small amounts and modify front[0..3] depth independently to break the y699/702/699 boundary. Candidate starting perturbations can be +2,-2,+1 m in height and +2,+4,+1 m in world Z for front[1,2,3] respectively, followed by actual screen reprojection. These values are experimental, not fit/acceptance criteria, and should be rejected if shoulder overlap or opening silhouette worsens.",
      "For a genuine broad grass ledge, prefer inserting one additional upper profile only across crown segments0..3 between the existing front boundary and lower face. Keep a rock riser and a shallow upper grass-facing surface, with unequal depths and heights. Preserve the existing external lower boundary and all closed side connections. Merely marking the steep face green repeats the failure.",
      "Do not widen the crown all the way to screen x1235 by assumption: western_slab also owns this left shoulder region. Preserve its production asset initially and judge overlap in Godot."
    ],
    "16b_minimal_suggestion": [
      "After isolated crown assessment, modify central_wall mid[1..3], front[1..3], ridge[1..3], all confirmed non-rim. Recess the middle channel in actual depth and offset adjacent wall breaks asymmetrically, instead of translating all five columns. A local Z displacement around -3 to -6 m at central mid[2] is a bounded starting experiment for a recessed groove; coordinate/render checks must decide the final value and whether neighboring upper points must follow.",
      "front_columns mid[1,2] and front[1,2] are confirmed non-rim and may form distinct ledges/wall bulges while the actual feet remain fixed. Preserve unequal cap depths rather than narrowing the whole cap. All duplicated GLB positions across normal/color splits must move together; authoring should target Blender source vertices.",
      "Use control projections from this JSON. In central_wall, ridge Z is clamped by min(frontZ-7); source input UVs1325/725,1377/717,1405/745 actually project to1319.299/721.314,1361.263/708.034,1390.525/736.447. Editing raw screen tuples without accounting for the clamp can miss the intended region."
    ],
    "ground_clamp_warning": "central shoulder[2,3] actual Y=44.666500,44.583538 and columns shoulder[0,2,3] Y=42.534584,41.170860,43.183544 are terrain-clamped and differ from nominal subtraction. Source recomputation uses terrain_topology ground_at, not a saved-scene GLB surface, so a full generator rerun can change contact rings despite intending an upper-only edit. Start from preserved native mesh or enforce exact frozen boundary; do not import the whole generator during this audit.",
    "not_solved_by_upper_only": [
      "Lower wall-foot contact silhouette, visible terrain color boundary, big dark triangular slopes, terrain cliff intersections, roads and vegetation remain outside an upper-only pass.",
      "A groove can terminate inside the model under a fixed rim. A true valley outlet at a changed footprint cannot be created while insisting the footprint/rim stay identical.",
      "Keeping rim fixed reduces dependencies but does not prove all new faces stay above terrain or avoid neighboring assets. Upper surface displacement can still create intersections; collisions must match the new mesh.",
      "The broad x1235-1415 shoulder involves adjacent western_slab and terrain; these three upper-control edits alone cannot guarantee reference fidelity."
    ],
    "validation_required": "Before/after exact local rim and floor coordinates, no new topology holes/degenerate triangles, same independent Blender/GLB/prefab ownership, fresh collision from candidate, opening/cliff-side/cliff-back raw GPU views of one version, then independent visual review. No GPU pixel-ownership or self-intersection proof was performed in this audit."
